<Layout
  title="Tiny Numbers Generator - Superscript & Subscript Digits | SmallTextGen"
  description="Convert numbers 0-9 and math symbols to superscript or subscript format. Complete digit mapping table. Perfect for dates, IDs, equations, and chemical formulas. Free tool."
  canonicalUrl="https://www.small-text-gen.com/tiny-numbers"
>
  <Fragment slot="extra-head">
 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebApplication","name":"Tiny Numbers Generator","url":"https://www.small-text-gen.com/tiny-numbers","description":"Convert numbers 0-9 into superscript or subscript Unicode digits. Includes math symbols. Free instant tool for dates, IDs, equations.","applicationCategory":"UtilityApplication","operatingSystem":"All","dateModified":"2026-08-11"}</script>
    <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can all numbers be converted to tiny format?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, all digits 0-9 have both superscript and subscript equivalents in Unicode. Math symbols +, -, =, (, ) also have tiny versions. This is one of the few character sets in Unicode with 100% coverage."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why do not other tools convert numbers?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most tools focus only on letter conversion. We built tiny numbers support after noticing users had to manually handle dates, IDs, and stats. It is a gap in the market we are happy to fill."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I mix tiny numbers with small text letters?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Use superscript letters with superscript numbers, or subscript letters with subscript numbers for a consistent look. Our main tool shows all 9 styles simultaneously."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use tiny numbers for math homework?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes for simple exponents, basic equations, and chemical formulas. For complex math, LaTeX is still preferred. Our tool is perfect for social media math and casual formatting."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do tiny numbers work on all platforms?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Unicode superscript and subscript digits 0-9 have universal support across iOS, Android, Windows, macOS, and all major apps. They were among the earliest characters in Unicode 1.0."}}]}</script>
